  "term": "self-transcendence",
  "definition": "In this historical Hegelian sense, self-transcendence is the way a fixed concept goes beyond itself because its internal opposition or contradiction shows that it cannot stand as an isolated ultimate idea. It names the movement by which thought passes toward a more comprehensive standpoint.",
